    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Door at [-39.8, -0.0, 2904.15]: BJX fork Battles.lua:18 (Npcs.json Id 46197, sh_cave_entrance_bat_cave_01.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region Briarwood, place Briarwood."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 16 ('Briarheart Caverns (the live dungeon: Hailstorm's changelings from the shrine through the caverns, Geomancer H'): scene bw_briarheart_caverns, entry, exit, 6 waves, 23 spawns ({'Changeling Hacker': 7, 'Changeling Marauder': 8, 'Changeling Berserker': 7, 'Geomancer Hailstorm': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1215 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene bw_briarheart_caverns has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 75 coins / 260 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier. Door actor 100000046197: reference Npcs.json Id 46197, model 251, name 5707, at [-39.8, -0.0, 2904.15]."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) The guide's main goal is the one goal shown from the start and is done with the fork's last goal; the steps before it stay, as the triggers of its waves and boss."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Guide overlay by scripts/dungeon_fights.py from data/content/dungeons/briarheart_caverns.json."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "rc-0137 prize wheel: fandom 'Briarheart Caverns' (revision 49146) lists one prize wheel per combat job and a 117-coin slot; any other job spins the items every job's wheel holds. Archer: the wiki's 'Pinhole Archer Boots' is 'Pin Hole Archer Boots' in our record dungeons/briarheart_caverns.json."
    }
